✅ Tech Stack Used in CivicPulse
🎨 Frontend (Client Side)
React (v19) – For building interactive user interface
Vite – Fast build tool and development server
Tailwind CSS (v4) – Utility-first styling for responsive design
React Router DOM – Navigation and routing between pages
Axios – For API communication with backend
Lucide React – Icons for UI enhancement
ESLint – Code quality and linting
⚙️ Backend (Server Side)
Node.js – JavaScript runtime for server-side development
Express.js (v5) – Web framework for building REST APIs
MongoDB Atlas – Cloud-based NoSQL database
Mongoose – ODM for MongoDB data modeling
🔐 Authentication & Security
JWT (JSON Web Token) – Secure authentication
bcryptjs – Password hashing
🛠️ Other Tools & Utilities
dotenv – Environment variable management
CORS – Handling cross-origin requests
Nodemon – Auto-restarting server during development
🎯 Final One-Line Answer (For Viva)

👉
“CivicPulse is built using the MERN stack with React 19, Vite, and Tailwind CSS
on the frontend, and Node.js, Express.js, and MongoDB with Mongoose on the backend,
along with JWT-based authentication.”